  "id": "COMPOUND:11458 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Flumedroxone is implicated in the biological activity of LNCaP through a series of molecular interactions that involve the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Ajugaciliatin E, Teyin, and Phorone, all of which are linked to the LNCaP cell line. The evidence suggests that Flumedroxone may act as a modulator of the SDR family, potentially influencing the activity of these targets. The shared target of LNCaP across these compounds implies a possible mechanism of action involving the SDR family, which could be relevant to the regulation of cellular processes in prostate cancer. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of SDR family members in mediating the effects of Flumedroxone on LNCaP, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
